          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાયદો — kāydo — \"a law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નવો કાયદો ગરીબ માણસો માટે સારો છે. navo kāydo garīb māṇso māṭe sāro che. The new law is good for poor people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાયદો (kāydo) is usually traced to Arabic qāʿida, \"a base, a rule\", through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
